nP still shows zero external USB devices on `USB\\ROOT_HUB30`, and guide/execute the exact step so the box enumerates on USB (`PID_4EE7` / `PID_0D02`) and completes the 4-step liberation flow (`1. Escanear la Memoria -> 2. Entrar en Modo Fastboot -> 3. Inyectar Firmware -> 4. Éxito Total`).\n- **Scope Boundaries & Mandatory Rules ([`REGLA_SIN_ABRIR_TORNILLOS_NO_TTL.md`](file:///c:/Users/andre/OneDrive/Desktop/xview/.agents/rules/REGLA_SIN_ABRIR_TORNILLOS_NO_TTL.md)):**\n  - **100% External (Zero UART TTL / Zero `SmarTTY` / Zero screws opened).**\n  - **Never mention or ask the user to click `Compilación` 7 times.**\n  - **Never flash `factory.img` (Widevine L1) or `cri_data.img` (MAC/Serial).**\n\n---\n\n### 2. Progress\n1. **Updated [`V2/B866v2 Android 12/B866v2 Android 12/B866V2-FlashATV12 - Evoca.bat`](file:///c:/Users/andre/OneDrive/Desktop/xview/V2/B866v2%20Android%2012/B866v2%20Android%2012/B866V2-FlashATV12%20-%20Evoca.bat) and [`programa perfecto/PROGRAMA_PERFECTO_XVIEW_B866V2.exe`](file:///c:/Users/andre/OneDrive/Desktop/xview/programa%20perfecto/PROGRAMA_PERFECTO_XVIEW_B866V2.exe) (`v4.1`):**\n   - Both automatically detect `fastbootd` (`PID_4EE7`, `is-userspace: yes`) and jump to `U-Boot Fastboot` (`PID_0D02`) via `fastboot reboot bootloader`, send EVOCA's exact unlock sequence (`fastboot oem 'setenv lock 10100000;save`), flash the safe Android 12 partitions (omitting `factory.img` and `cri_data.img`), and maintain an Anti-Watchdog `:KEEP_ALIVE` loop.\n2. **Disassembled [`experimento/11_VALIDACION_OTA_Y_FIRMWARE_ZTE/system_bin_recovery`](file:///c:/Users/andre/OneDrive/Desktop/xview/experimento/11_VALIDACION_OTA_Y_FIRMWARE_ZTE/system_bin_recovery) (`recovery_main.cpp` `0xB06A0..0xB4D00` and `recovery.cpp` `0xB4D00..0xB8000`):**\n   - Extracted exact Thumb2 `LDR + ADD PC` cross-references (`[ExactXref]` and `[RecoveryDump]`):\n     - `0xB1D4A` (`vaddr 0xB2D4A` in `recovery_main.cpp`): `\"Entering fastboot\"` (`0x31704`) — **does NOT call `SetUSBDevice`!** It only sets `sys.usb.config=fastboot` (`0xB1CF8`).\n     - `0xB4F10` (`vaddr 0xB5F10` in `recovery.cpp`): `\"SetUSBHost \"` (`0x34459`).\n     - `0xB4F4C` (`vaddr 0xB5F4C` in `recovery.cpp`): `\"SetUSBDevice \"` (`0x37EFD`).\n     - `0xB6946..0xB69D0` (`vaddr 0xB7946..0xB79D0` in `recovery.cpp`): Writes `ubootenv.var.otg_device` to `/dev/block/env`, prints `\"Set USB Status Success!\"`, and shows the prompt `\"Reboot System Now?\"`.\n3. **Live Hardware & PnP Check After User Said `\"listo toma el control nuevamente\"`:**\n   - Checked `Get-PnpDevice -PresentOnly`, `fastboot_moderno.exe devices -l`, `fastboot.exe devices -l`, `adb.exe devices -l`, `adnl.exe devices`, `update.exe identify 7`, `arp -a`, and [`BITACORA_EN_VIVO_EXE.log`](file:///c:/Users/andre/OneDrive/Desktop/xview/programa%20perfecto/BITACORA_EN_VIVO_EXE.log).\n   - Confirmed `PROGRAMA_PERFECTO_XVIEW_B866V2.exe v4.1` (`PID=20608`) is still running in `[PASO 2/4] ENTRANDO EN MODO FASTBOOT...` and `USB\\ROOT_HUB30` still shows zero external USB devices connected.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Key Findings\n1. **Critical Discovery from Disassembling `system_bin_recovery` (`0xB1D4A` vs `0xB4F4C..0xB69D0`):**\n   - Earlier we hypothesized that `\"Entering fastboot\"` (`0x31704`) called `SetUSBDevice` (`otg_device=1`). **Our exact Thumb2 XREF dump proved that was false!**\n   - In `recovery_main.cpp` (`0xB1D4A`), `\"Entering fastboot\"` only sets `sys.usb.config = fastboot`. It **never** touches `ubootenv.var.otg_device`!\n   - Instead, `ubootenv.var.otg_device` (`0xB6946`) is **ONLY** modified in `recovery.cpp` (`0xB4F4C`) when the user is in **`Android Recovery`** (by selecting **`Enter recovery`** from `fastbootd`) and selects **`Set USB device`** from the Recovery menu, which prints `\"Set USB Status Success!\"` (`0xB696A`) and asks **`\"Reboot System Now?\"`** (`0xB69D0`)!\n2. **Why `Reboot to bootloader` from `fastbootd` Did Not Enumerate on the PC (2 Exact Causes):**\n   - **Cause A (If this is a new box or `otg_device=0`):** Selecting `Reboot to bootloader` while `KINGSTON` (`factory_update_param.aml` = `--fastboot`) is still plugged into the box causes U-Boot (`Command: bcb uboot-command`) to read `boot-recovery` / `factory_update_param.aml` and boot right back into `fastbootd` (or if `KINGSTON` is removed, it enters `U-Boot Fastboot` for only ~8 seconds before the hardware watchdog `ffd0f0d0.watchdog` resets it if the USB cable isn't on the right port). And if `otg_device=0`, `fastbootd` never turns on USB until **`Enter recovery` $\\rightarrow$ `Set USB device` $\\rightarrow$ `Yes`** is executed!\n   - **Cause B (Physical USB Port Swap on the Box):** On the ZTE B866V2 (`board_id=8`), only **ONE** of the two USB ports is wired to the **USB OTG controller (`dwc2_a` / `PID_4EE7` / `PID_0D02` / `PID_4EE1`)**, while the other USB port is **Host-only** (for the `KINGSTON` flash drive). Earlier at `01:07`–`01:12` AM (`BITACORA_EN_VIVO_EXE.log` lines 235–380), box `Z41220090388172` enumerated in `PID_4EE7`, `PID_0D02`, and `PID_4EE1` (MTP in normal Android). If the `KINGSTON` USB drive is currently plugged into the OTG port and the USB Male-to-Male cable is plugged into the other port, Windows `USB\\ROOT_HUB30` receives **zero signal** in all modes (`Android`, `fastbootd`, and `Bootloader`).\n\n---\n\n### 4. Errors & Fixes\n- **Error 1: `fastboot.exe` path error when checking `platform-tools\\fastboot.exe`:**\n  - *Root cause:* In `programa perfecto\\1_HERRAMIENTAS_MOTOR`, `fastboot.exe` and `fastboot_moderno.exe` are directly in `1_HERRAMIENTAS_MOTOR\\`, not in a `platform-tools` subfolder.\n  - *Fix:* Used `1_HERRAMIENTAS_MOTOR\\fastboot_moderno.exe` and `1_HERRAMIENTAS_MOTOR\\fastboot.exe`.\n- **Error 2: `Select-String` across `experimento\\*\\*` hit directory read errors on `03_configuraciones_etc\\*`:**\n  - *Root cause:* Subdirectories matched `*` without `-File`.\n  - *Fix:* Targeted specific `.log`, `.md`, and `.txt` files.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Active Context\n- **Running B